{number: 153}
{title: Because He Lives}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] God sent His Son, they called Him [Db] Jesus;
He came to [Ab] heal, love and for-[Eb7] give;
He lived and [Ab] died to buy my [Db] pardon,
An empty [Ab] grave is there to [Eb7] prove my Savior [Ab] lives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Because He [Ab] lives, I can face to-[Db] morrow,
Because He [Ab] lives, all fear is [Eb7] gone;
Because I [Ab] know He holds the [Db] future,
And life is [Ab] worth the living [Eb7] just because He [Ab] lives.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
How [Ab] sweet to hold a newborn [Db] baby
And feel the [Ab] pride and joy he [Eb7] gives;
But greater [Ab] still the calm as-[Db] surance:
This child can [Ab] face uncertain [Eb7] days because Christ [Ab] lives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [Ab] then one day I'll cross the [Db] river,
I'll fight life's [Ab] final war with [Eb7] pain;
And then, as [Ab] death gives way to [Db] victory,
I'll see the [Ab] lights of glory [Eb7] and I'll know He [Ab] lives.
{end_of_verse}
